WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:09.280
For the rest of the day, Daisy and Kaleem tried to find a home for Scamp.

2
00:00:09.281 --> 00:00:28.173
They knocked on every door in the neighborhood.

3
00:00:28.174 --> 00:00:32.619
Many of the neighbors knew Scamp and liked him.

4
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:36.279
But nobody would adopt him.

5
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:41.180
"I'm sorry, but my cats wouldn't approve," a man said.

6
00:00:41.181 --> 00:00:44.399
A pair of cats stared out from behind him.

7
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.962
"Right," one said. "We don't like dogs."

8
00:00:48.963 --> 00:00:52.358
Daisy wanted to tell the cats that Scamp was nice.

9
00:00:52.359 --> 00:00:55.358
But she couldn't do it in front of their owner.

10
00:00:55.359 --> 00:01:04.793
Besides, how would she convince the owner without giving away her secret?

11
00:01:04.794 --> 00:01:11.199
"I wish I could tell people that I can talk to animals," she said as they walked away from the house.

12
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.848
"Maybe then they'd understand how upset Scamp is and adopt him."

13
00:01:15.849 --> 00:01:19.447
"What? No!" Beatrice sounded alarmed.

14
00:01:19.448 --> 00:01:21.600
"You can't tell anyone, Daisy!

15
00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:24.025
Besides, you know how adults are.

16
00:01:24.026 --> 00:01:28.244
They'll think you're playing a silly game and never believe you."

17
00:01:28.245 --> 00:01:30.321
Daisy sighed.

18
00:01:30.322 --> 00:01:33.256
Beatrice was so confusing sometimes.

19
00:01:33.257 --> 00:01:37.187
But right now she had a bigger problem to solve.

20
00:01:37.188 --> 00:01:44.015
"Kaleem, let's try the next house."

21
00:01:44.016 --> 00:01:59.653
By Sunday, they still hadn't found a home for Scamp.

22
00:01:59.654 --> 00:02:05.231
Daisy and Kaleem met in her backyard after breakfast.

23
00:02:05.232 --> 00:02:09.044
"I don't know what to do," she said.

24
00:02:09.045 --> 00:02:14.019
"Poor Scamp! I guess he's going with the rescue group tomorrow."

25
00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:16.833
Beatrice buzzed over.

26
00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:22.711
"You can't give up, Daisy. Keep thinking. Time is running out!"

27
00:02:22.712 --> 00:02:26.457
"Let's visit Mrs. Ortiz in the hospital," Kaleem said.

28
00:02:26.458 --> 00:02:35.083
"Maybe she'll have some ideas."

29
00:02:35.084 --> 00:02:42.289
Kaleem's dad dropped them off at the hospital.

30
00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:51.213
He was going to park the car and wait for them.

31
00:02:51.214 --> 00:02:58.363
"You're Grace's friends!" Mrs. Ortiz said when the kids entered.

32
00:02:58.364 --> 00:03:02.219
"Thank you for looking after Scamp."

33
00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.821
"We've been trying to find a home for him."

34
00:03:04.822 --> 00:03:10.267
Daisy told Mrs. Ortiz about talking to Grace's parents and the neighbors.

35
00:03:10.268 --> 00:03:12.733
Mrs. Ortiz looked sad.

36
00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:18.809
"I wish I could keep him, even though he'll be happier with someone younger.

37
00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:25.204
I was hoping Grace would adopt him. But Scamp can't be around those fish.

38
00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:29.356
And that tank is already a lot of work."

39
00:03:29.357 --> 00:03:32.365
"We were hoping that too," Daisy said.

40
00:03:32.366 --> 00:03:39.659
Mrs. Ortiz sighed. "I'm sorry for the stress this will cause him.

41
00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:45.101
And I must admit, I'm feeling a little sorry for myself too."

42
00:03:45.102 --> 00:03:48.833
"You mean because you'll miss Scamp?" Kaleem asked.

43
00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:55.404
The old woman nodded. "Yes. I've always had an animal or two around.

44
00:03:55.405 --> 00:04:00.251
I'm looking forward to seeing more of my grandkids.

45
00:04:00.252 --> 00:04:04.728
But they'll be at school all day, and their parents will be at work.

46
00:04:04.729 --> 00:04:10.110
I'm afraid I'll be terribly bored in that condo by myself."

47
00:04:10.111 --> 00:04:12.185
She glanced toward the window.

48
00:04:12.186 --> 00:04:15.521
"I suppose I'll have to settle for bird-watching.

49
00:04:15.522 --> 00:04:20.405
But that's not the same as being able to fuss over a pet of your own.

50
00:04:20.406 --> 00:04:25.733
I like taking care of something. Maybe I'll get some fish."

51
00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:28.819
Daisy gasped. "No!"

52
00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:32.980
Kaleem looked surprised. "What do you have against fish?"

53
00:04:32.981 --> 00:04:36.565
"It's not that. I have an even better idea."

54
00:04:36.566 --> 00:04:39.575
Daisy smiled at Mrs. Ortiz.

55
00:04:39.576 --> 00:04:47.929
"We have to go now. But I'm hoping I'll be back soon with good news!"

